                </paragraph>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="block">$$f(x) = \frac{1}{x\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}$$</math>
                </paragraph>
                <paragraph>
                  What is the domain of <math display="inline">$$f$$</math> and <math display="inline">$$F$$</math> ?
                </paragraph>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$$- \ln\left| \frac{1 + \sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}{x} \right| + C$$</math> ; both have domain <math display="inline">$$\left( {- 1,0} \right) \cup \left( {0,1} \right)$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  Use mathematical software to evaluate <math display="inline">$$F(x)$$</math> . What is the domain of the function <math display="inline">$$F$$</math> that the software produces? Is there a discrepancy between this domain and the domain of the function <math display="inline">$$F$$</math> that you found in part (a)?
                </paragraph>
              </item>
            </list>
          </statement>
