  <subsection title="Discovery Project Patterns in Integrals">
    <paragraph>
      In this project mathematical software is used to investigate indefinite integrals of families of functions. By observing the patterns that occur in the integrals of several members of the family, you will first guess, and then prove, a general formula for the integral of any member of the family.
    </paragraph>
    <list ordered="true">
      <item>
        <list ordered="true">
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Use a computer to evaluate the following integrals.
            </paragraph>
            <list ordered="true">
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int\frac{1}{\left( {x + 2} \right)\left( {x + 3} \right)}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int\frac{1}{\left( {x + 1} \right)\left( {x + 5} \right)}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int\frac{1}{\left( {x + 2} \right)\left( {x - 5} \right)}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int\frac{1}{\left( {x + 2} \right)^{2}}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
            </list>
          </item>
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Based on the pattern of your responses in part (a), guess the value of the integral
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph>
              <math display="block">$${\int\frac{1}{\left( {x + a} \right)\left( {x + b} \right)}}dx$$</math>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph>
              if <math display="inline">$$a \neq b$$</math> . What if <math display="inline">$$a = b$$</math> ?
            </paragraph>
          </item>
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Check your guess by using the software to evaluate the integral in part (b). Then prove it using partial fractions.
            </paragraph>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <list ordered="true">
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Use a computer to evaluate the following integrals.
            </paragraph>
            <list ordered="true">
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{\sin x\cos 2x}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{\sin 3x\cos 7x}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{\sin 8x\cos 3x}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
            </list>
          </item>
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Based on the pattern of your responses in part (a), guess the value of the integral
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph>
              <math display="block">$${\int{\sin ax\cos bx}}dx$$</math>
            </paragraph>
          </item>
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Check your guess with the computer. Then prove it using the techniques of Section 7.2. For what values of <math display="inline">$$a$$</math> and <math display="inline">$$b$$</math> is it valid?
            </paragraph>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <list ordered="true">
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Use a computer to evaluate the following integrals.
            </paragraph>
            <list ordered="true">
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{\ln x}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{x\ln x}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{x^{2}\ln x}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{x^{3}\ln x}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{x^{7}\ln x}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
            </list>
          </item>
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Based on the pattern of your responses in part (a), guess the value of
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph>
              <math display="block">$${\int{x^{n}\ln x}}dx$$</math>
            </paragraph>
          </item>
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Use integration by parts to prove the conjecture that you made in part (b). For what values of <math display="inline">$$n$$</math> is it valid?
            </paragraph>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <list ordered="true">
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Use a computer to evaluate the following integrals.
            </paragraph>
            <list ordered="true">
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{xe^{ x}}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{x^{2}e^{ x}}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{x^{3}e^{ x}}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{x^{4}e^{ x}}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="inline">$${\int{x^{5}e^{ x}}}dx$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
            </list>
          </item>
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Based on the pattern of your responses in part (a), guess the value of <math display="inline">$${\int{x^{6}e^{ x}}}dx$$</math> . Then use the computer to check your guess.
            </paragraph>
          </item>
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Based on the patterns in parts (a) and (b), make a conjecture as to the value of the integral
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph>
              <math display="block">$${\int{x^{n}e^{ x}}}dx$$</math>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph>
              when <math display="inline">$$n$$</math> is a positive integer.
            </paragraph>
          </item>
          <item>
            <paragraph>
              Use mathematical induction to prove the conjecture you made in part (c)
            </paragraph>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </subsection>
